WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.720
Tuesday night. The farm walk's done,

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.510
the covers are on your phone,

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.960
nobody checked the
rain gauge on Monday,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.710
and a kill sheet's just
landed in your inbox.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.480
Paste your notes into
ChatGPT, Copilot,

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.900
Gemini or Claude and ask for a table.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.460
In seconds you've got every
paddock sorted by cover,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.850
in kilograms of dry
matter per hectare,

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.400
ready for the feed wedge.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.820
Ask it to show the sum
and what it divided by,

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.410
and you can check the average
on your phone in ten seconds.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.540
Here's the catch.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.640
The paddock you didn't walk
can come back as zero,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.350
and the average drops to a cover
that still looks believable.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.060
Thursday's forecast gets added to
the rain that's already fallen.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.070
On the kill sheet, a condemned
carcass slips into the average

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.040
and a downgrade note disappears.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.760
So check every number against its row.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.200
Ask for the paddocks or
tags behind each figure.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.960
A blank means not
recorded, never zero,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.040
and a forecast stays a forecast.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.160
Before you paste anything,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.070
check the tool's data settings,

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.520
and leave out what
the job doesn't need,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.090
like staff phone numbers
and health notes.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.160
Next, check an AI summary of a kill
sheet against the sheet itself.
